WEBVTT

00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:03.031
First, tidal volume.

00:00:03.081 --> 00:00:06.531
That's the air you move in and out with a normal, quiet breath.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.265
So we'll breathe normally, and capture just one breath.

00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:12.350
Take a normal breath in.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.039
Now breathe out normally into the balloon. Don't force it.

00:00:20.489 --> 00:00:22.603
Pinch the neck so no air escapes.

00:00:23.653 --> 00:00:24.717
Now measure.

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:28.557
The diameter is about 10 centimeters.

00:00:29.407 --> 00:00:31.752
Say the number out loud as you read it.

00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:34.800
Let's do it a second time, quickly.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.862
Normal breath in.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:38.814
Normal breath out.

00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:40.460
Pinch.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.490
Measure.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.111
About 9.5 centimeters.

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:48.520
Write down each number. We'll average the trials in a moment.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.775
Tidal volume is the smallest of the three amounts we'll measure.

00:00:55.153 --> 00:00:57.723
Next, expiratory reserve volume.

00:00:57.773 --> 00:01:01.765
That's the extra air you can still push out, after a normal breath out.

00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:05.064
This one is tricky, so watch closely.

00:01:05.514 --> 00:01:08.454
Take a normal breath in, and breathe out normally.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:15.561
Now, without breathing in, blow all the extra air into the balloon, and pinch it.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.894
Do NOT take a breath in between!

00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:25.814
Here's what goes wrong. If you breathe in first, you add new air.

00:01:27.465 --> 00:01:32.210
The balloon comes out too big, and that number isn't your expiratory reserve volume.

00:01:34.061 --> 00:01:37.995
So breathe out normally, then blow out the extra air. Measure.

00:01:38.645 --> 00:01:40.356
About 12 centimeters.

00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:44.658
Last, vital capacity.

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:47.358
That's the most air you can move in one breath.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:51.068
It's the biggest breath of all, so take your time.

00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:53.484
Take the deepest breath you can.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.487
Now blow it all out into the balloon.

00:02:02.138 --> 00:02:04.919
Keep going until you can't push out any more air.

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:07.377
Pinch it, and measure.

00:02:08.426 --> 00:02:10.306
About 18 centimeters.

00:02:10.957 --> 00:02:13.758
Notice how much bigger the balloon is this time.

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:17.325
Vital capacity is the largest of the three.
